// WALKBCN_SM_TEXT[lang][id], same shape in every language (scripts/check.mjs compares them).
// Every fact comes from WalkBCN's checked stop stories and cards (sources listed per mission);
// only the framing note in `intro` is fiction, and the page labels it as such.
// Steps: missions[0..2] are places (location check, then a question); step 3 is the final
// deduction. `answers` = index of the right option per step, also stored in the SQL
// (mp_challenges.answers) so the server checks answers; check.mjs compares both.
// Clues: each mission has 4 clues; clue j goes to player (j + mission) % players, so clues 0 and 1,
// which are both needed for the question, always go to different players.
